    // ---- CLIFF ROCK -------------------------------------------------------
    // A SECOND STONE, not a treatment of the first. Everything above is the
    // slope wash: warm, low-contrast, metre-bedded, right for a weathered
    // flank. A face that stands at 60-75 degrees does so because it spalls,
    // and spalled rock is darker, cooler and carries its bedding as hard
    // horizontal breaks. Sharing one albedo between the two is what made a
    // wall read as the same paint as the meadow above it.
    //
